{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/choule99\/swift-snapshot-testing"},{"type":"text","text":" writes the snapshots it generates directly to disk"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alongside the test files. This makes for compact test cases with single line assertions…"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["assertSnapshot(of: value, as: .json)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"…but can make verification more cumbersome: one must find the corresponding file in order to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"verify that it matches their expectation. In this case, if the above assertion is the second one in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"code":"testMySnapshot()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"MySnapshotTests.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file, the snapshot will be found at:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["$ cat __Snapshots__\/MySnapshotTests\/testMySnapshot.2.json","{","  \"id\": 42,","  \"name\": \"Blob\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inline Snapshot Testing offers an alternative approach by writing string snapshots directly into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the test file. This makes it easy to verify a snapshot test at any time, since the value and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot sit next to each other in the assertion. One can "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import InlineSnapshotTesting"},{"type":"text","text":" and rewrite"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the above assertion as:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["assertInlineSnapshot(of: value, as: .json)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"And when the test is run, it will automatically insert the snapshot as a trailing closure to be used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by future test runs, and fail:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["assertInlineSnapshot(of: value, as: .json) {  \/\/ ❌","  \"\"\"","  {","    \"id\": 42,","    \"name\": \"Blob\"","  }","  \"\"\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"code":["❌ failed - Automatically recorded a new snapshot.","","Re-run \"testMySnapshot\" to test against the newly-recorded snapshot."],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"style":"warning","name":"Warning","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When a snapshot is written into a test file, the undo history of the test file in Xcode","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"will be lost. Be careful to avoid losing work, and commit often to version control.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"We would love for this to be fixed. Please ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.apple.com\/feedback\/","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" with Apple to improve","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"things, or if you have an idea of how we can improve things from the library, please","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/choule99\/swift-snapshot-testing\/discussions","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/choule99\/swift-snapshot-testing\/pulls","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/inlinesnapshottesting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"InlineSnapshotTesting"}],"externalID":"InlineSnapshotTesting","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"InlineSnapshotTesting"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift",